menu "IR capture (RMT RX)"

    config IR_CAPTURE_GLITCH_FILTER_NS
        int "Glitch filter (ns)"
        range 0 10000
        default 1000
        help
            Pulses shorter than this are discarded as noise. The shortest pulse in
            common IR protocols is around 300 us, so 1 us is a safe filter.

    config IR_CAPTURE_FRAME_GAP_MS
        int "End-of-frame idle gap (ms)"
        range 5 32
        default 25
        help
            Reception stops when one level persists longer than this, which marks
            the end of the frame. At the 1 MHz channel resolution the hardware
            ceiling is 32.767 ms, so larger values are rejected by the driver.

    config IR_CAPTURE_LEARN_WINDOW_MS
        int "Default learn inactivity window (ms)"
        range 1000 60000
        default 15000
        help
            Default value used by the bring-up flow. Every captured frame restarts
            the window, so several buttons can be learned in one session.

    config IR_CAPTURE_DEDUP_WINDOW_MS
        int "Repeat de-duplication window (ms)"
        range 50 2000
        default 400
        help
            A frame arriving within this time of the previous one is reported as a
            repeat instead of a new frame. Helps both full-frame repeats and short
            repeat codes (for example NEC).

    config IR_CAPTURE_MATCH_TOLERANCE_PERCENT
        int "Frame match relative tolerance (percent)"
        range 0 50
        default 15
        help
            Allowed deviation of a duration relative to the shorter of the two
            durations being compared.

    config IR_CAPTURE_MATCH_TOLERANCE_US
        int "Frame match absolute tolerance (us)"
        range 0 500
        default 100
        help
            Absolute deviation always accepted in addition to the relative
            tolerance, so that very short durations still compare reliably.

    config IR_CAPTURE_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Capture task priority"
        range 1 20
        default 10

    config IR_CAPTURE_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Capture task stack size (bytes)"
        range 2048 8192
        default 3072
        help
            The heavy buffers live in static storage, so the stack only needs to
            cover the call chain. 3 KB leaves comfortable headroom.

endmenu
